#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091970 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cb7d8dc0-98eb-53d0-9e48-3b1c2d7f6308" :question/math-academy-id "e-4508" :question/problem "Find a solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=2 \\\\ 4x+3y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/843dcd4359e4b61eb9715966fbbe6c26363ab5cfc57c55f94b6a41a73ec7feb1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/b9ba240f93ee3ec8c02e9718d62342dca0e0855e24c7b34ed97758a6eb7c46b8.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091971 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/id #uuid "422d31ad-8caa-5ce2-a0e0-c905fcc2640d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4509" :question/problem "Solve the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 6y-5x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $A\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/240a1d2f7f93ec808127c9fa1791a77a43fcd7c0c84505540acc81c8b9fbc6e1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/7850cbafc78f2cf2ce14ae7111064bf2f5a029f4d1b97b6d5ebfc09e7126f44e.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05c963c1-98e9-5a2d-a5c7-0f6d04dbda30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291758} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c36bc2-4930-5d0c-9a5f-14d8dcb8f959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291759} {:answer/id #uuid "590404f5-f3f8-532b-aeb2-8ac76e440df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291760} {:answer/id #uuid "796acc5c-1913-5743-9dd1-c48bcd03d333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291761} {:answer/id #uuid "850318a6-1a4d-5307-b80c-b8e0f486b5e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "796acc5c-1913-5743-9dd1-c48bcd03d333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291761} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca356f0b-e266-5dae-b876-0c22bbf0bfe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "95af1977-8d23-5d4e-89a9-245a921e273b" :question/math-academy-id "q-102806" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5=2x-3y \\\\ 4x=y-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 4x-y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330186 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "571cda49-691f-54cd-909d-41956e6a9d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330188} {:answer/id #uuid "f168c34a-0165-59f0-ba93-3fd17d37f1b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330189} {:answer/id #uuid "26178178-3495-55dc-a1b1-4e6f23f2a1c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330190} {:answer/id #uuid "e1bad37e-423c-5cd2-a707-21736c38c5f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330191} {:answer/id #uuid "b4fbfcf7-d44d-54d0-a813-8bd0c00533f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "571cda49-691f-54cd-909d-41956e6a9d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330188} :answer-field/id #uuid "d85225e6-0667-5788-9d20-4a0a21c245a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f0b10b3a-1c60-596e-980b-5212c6a85533" :question/math-academy-id "q-102807" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y=x+3 \\\\ 7-y=-x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-x+2y=3 \\\\ x-y=-7.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284734 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efc9c5fb-366e-58cc-800c-cc96a8f541ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284736} {:answer/id #uuid "01755979-0354-5a8c-8358-06db0e668a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284737} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a1d318-b9c1-5dee-a68e-573efd3017fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284738} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ecfbe4-3a59-5c01-b930-32e7ac659265" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284739} {:answer/id #uuid "58ddedb4-aea2-53f6-b4c4-c995257df447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01755979-0354-5a8c-8358-06db0e668a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284737} :answer-field/id #uuid "24ac07c7-8f78-5bfe-8981-b98603a3d774" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "174955d4-f9c8-5173-abe1-fa5e22029d62" :question/math-academy-id "q-102809" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x=1-3y \\\\ 3-4y=2x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x+3y=1 \\\\ -2x-4y=-3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-4)-(-2)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23aadfeb-a12f-5d04-8b68-8a411f75a314" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23aadfeb-a12f-5d04-8b68-8a411f75a314" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330195} :answer-field/id #uuid "cae55a35-a19f-521b-bcd4-5925d2ba7970" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330194} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2685e309-bf99-590c-82a6-a1618faa329f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2685e309-bf99-590c-82a6-a1618faa329f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330197} :answer-field/id #uuid "33ded688-a456-57c1-bd1b-2b0d24950199" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330196} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1450bd91-6e46-5270-8f1e-81be3169bc11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1450bd91-6e46-5270-8f1e-81be3169bc11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330199} :answer-field/id #uuid "85e7cf31-5e64-5d90-8440-bdf300bd09ca" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9197a66d-6982-5b0a-b6b2-5e26098bb7cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-275758" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4x+2y=-1 \\\\ x-3y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $2$ |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-4)\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330200 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c400020f-e6da-55bc-967a-f8d955e6aede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c400020f-e6da-55bc-967a-f8d955e6aede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330202} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec87351c-1da9-51e1-8034-8ce932a81d90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330201} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbb32358-bc57-5a2a-8f4b-64778c96fef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbb32358-bc57-5a2a-8f4b-64778c96fef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330204} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8f60af5-c4a5-5f21-9325-062b02927d5e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330203} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b765a90-99ed-59c1-b4df-dbd5b8aa7a77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b765a90-99ed-59c1-b4df-dbd5b8aa7a77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330206} :answer-field/id #uuid "497a0375-f3a5-5b20-ad7d-5f9faaf74894" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2837283f-7c61-55d2-a393-6b0e82a34b4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-275763" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3y=1-3x \\\\ x-2=-4y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $1$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $2$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+3y=1 \\\\ x+4y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092625 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f4cb845-21e2-5be5-8103-9bca7bdc80ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330208} {:answer/id #uuid "c66fdf1d-7421-5f7a-8d36-fd5639101bc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330209} {:answer/id #uuid "3bcd729f-67b1-58de-9a0d-c106cbd9b9f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330210} {:answer/id #uuid "b9efaf71-ea95-54a3-8dcb-8cc68348d07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330211} {:answer/id #uuid "db668378-0147-5c01-adc5-e6785a1ea573" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c66fdf1d-7421-5f7a-8d36-fd5639101bc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330209} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f56a54b-86da-5a7b-8608-50c7b4e271d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6d30370-c2bc-519b-ba0f-95ca534628ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-31893" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=1 \\\\ 2x+2y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25048217-1dfc-5bc0-bcf0-dd26866d663d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330215} {:answer/id #uuid "ce3c6099-ca47-56ea-9ea5-2ec3419a475a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce3c6099-ca47-56ea-9ea5-2ec3419a475a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330216} :answer-field/id #uuid "d11e8dc3-a9e4-5776-bef5-342369c777ac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330214} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffaaa5ed-41e1-5c58-b2fa-b3b13e51bde2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffaaa5ed-41e1-5c58-b2fa-b3b13e51bde2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330218} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffc0d0c1-cf74-5cbf-a05d-18701c0999e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330217} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "407a41f1-cca9-5067-a8c8-d4dea09cf587" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "407a41f1-cca9-5067-a8c8-d4dea09cf587" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330220} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc389450-8abe-51a6-9a60-b5f336196028" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330219}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7b8a9973-aa98-512e-bbfe-9875029cb267" :question/math-academy-id "q-320792" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 4x+y=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $1$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $2$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-2$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-2$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01681ac2-e161-567b-8a45-b934df1d456b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286343} {:answer/id #uuid "5121d015-f1d8-52bf-9d65-0cea17480a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5121d015-f1d8-52bf-9d65-0cea17480a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286344} :answer-field/id #uuid "32cde33b-9de2-5a38-ab81-1e07d7256b1a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286342} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cb5c507-528b-50a5-8985-9c5fa03c23e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cb5c507-528b-50a5-8985-9c5fa03c23e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286346} :answer-field/id #uuid "de5432b9-fedd-5640-9faf-47c1ca67c1e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286345} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2808ac36-e8ac-5295-9c1f-d84ef7b7493c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2808ac36-e8ac-5295-9c1f-d84ef7b7493c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286348} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7f1347f-288e-5404-8433-c1128330b84b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a1ccae0e-0d02-5cab-8336-a50181fa21a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-320805" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=7 \\\\ 5x+2y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $7$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-3$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3617b737-372f-57a3-9354-e1f76ea949a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330223} {:answer/id #uuid "4308187a-c5f2-5ccc-b692-bb8e101e7b28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330224} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2f43a7-7ccd-5bc2-a24b-35d8950ff15e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330225} {:answer/id #uuid "9dee7566-5c1a-57d4-b738-1dbf55247fa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330226} {:answer/id #uuid "54c4dad6-dbe1-5a56-bc07-19a7ff12f298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3617b737-372f-57a3-9354-e1f76ea949a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330223} :answer-field/id #uuid "4781c7d6-1b61-53b0-bdab-ccb9a3e7f865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330222}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f4f940f-f96d-53c6-8cdf-518ab4902f8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-32138" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x-y=17 \\\\ x+4y=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93d5301e-cdac-549c-8b27-594042eb57ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93d5301e-cdac-549c-8b27-594042eb57ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284786} :answer-field/id #uuid "b41db4be-d748-5c7d-8931-5326da2c7d9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284785} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca77f706-eb7e-571a-bc3b-9e44b9fffd37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca77f706-eb7e-571a-bc3b-9e44b9fffd37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284788} :answer-field/id #uuid "4462897a-eb59-5abc-b1f3-121e26a7dc7f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9f28575-101d-5daa-b849-50e5193c23df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9f28575-101d-5daa-b849-50e5193c23df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284790} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b5daf6a-5623-5507-8669-9845e20e3155" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "44824f47-f8c3-52d7-9631-687da781e31e" :question/math-academy-id "q-321439" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x=3+y \\\\ 5y=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $10$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $3$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $10$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x-y=3 \\\\ 0x+5y=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 5-0\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
